window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-062.json",{"day":62,"title":"Reading a Warning Before Sharing It","targetWords":[{"word":"typical","gloss":"典型的","context":"A typical message in a virtual neighborhood chat group claimed that an extreme storm would destroy the city's water supply.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"worldwide","gloss":"全世界的","context":"The warning spread worldwide through similar networks, even though its initial source was obscure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"rare","gloss":"稀少的","context":"The change was rare enough to attract attention, yet its meaning was profound.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"extreme","gloss":"极端","context":"A typical message in a virtual neighborhood chat group claimed that an extreme storm would destroy the city's water supply.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"cool","gloss":"冷静的","context":"One resident, Nora, remained cool enough to ask where and when it had been taken.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"relevant","gloss":"相关的","context":"Members compared raw reports with relevant public records and asked whether each conclusion was valid.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"vital","gloss":"重要的","context":"Nora thought it vital to avoid humiliating people, because embarrassed users might retreat into private groups where corrections never arrived.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"mere","gloss":"仅仅的","context":"A mere correction would not address this problem.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"opposite","gloss":"相反的","context":"A picture could be authentic while its suggested meaning was the opposite of the truth.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"remote","gloss":"遥远的","context":"A convenient search revealed that the tower stood in a remote country.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"weak","gloss":"弱的","context":"A weak network could transmit messages quickly but still fail badly at helping people understand them.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"usual","gloss":"通常的","context":"Constant changes in public advice had weakened confidence, and the usual official response often seemed thin on practical detail.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"constant","gloss":"坚定的","context":"Constant changes in public advice had weakened confidence, and the usual official response often seemed thin on practical detail.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"virtual","gloss":"虚拟","context":"A typical message in a virtual neighborhood chat group claimed that an extreme storm would destroy the city's water supply.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"inevitable","gloss":"不可避免的","context":"Some confusion was inevitable, although its consequences could be reduced through patient, consistent public communication.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":{"en":"an inevitable consequence","zh":"不可避免的后果"}},{"word":"brief","gloss":"简短的","context":"A tall photograph of a damaged tower looked genuine, and a brief caption described a permanent collapse.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"empty","gloss":"空的","context":"An empty statement that a claim was wrong was less useful than an explanation of why.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"excellent","gloss":"优秀的","context":"The local water system was stable, and the city had issued an excellent explanation of its emergency preparations.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"convenient","gloss":"方便的","context":"A convenient search revealed that the tower stood in a remote country.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"vulnerable","gloss":"易受攻击的","context":"However, Nora understood why vulnerable residents believed the false account.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":{"en":"vulnerable groups","zh":"弱势群体"}},{"word":"accurate","gloss":"精确的","context":"Her simple question exposed the difference between an alarming appearance and accurate information.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"odd","gloss":"奇数的","context":"Often it involved checking dates, contacting a named organization, or noticing an odd geographical detail.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"raw","gloss":"原始的","context":"Members compared raw reports with relevant public records and asked whether each conclusion was valid.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"flexible","gloss":"灵活的","context":"Nora invited a volunteer group to prepare a flexible guide for checking urgent claims.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"contrary","gloss":"相反的","context":"Contrary to popular expectations, verification did not always require radical technology.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"evil","gloss":"邪恶的","context":"The guide also warned against treating every mistaken sender as evil.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"solid","gloss":"固体的","context":"These small steps provided a solid basis for judgment without asking ordinary people to become professional investigators.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"adequate","gloss":"充足的","context":"Reliable communication needed adequate information about specific risks, delivered in a form that diverse audiences could understand.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sharp","gloss":"尖的","context":"A sharp distinction emerged between a minor error and a crucial omission.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"stable","gloss":"稳定的","context":"The local water system was stable, and the city had issued an excellent explanation of its emergency preparations.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"false","gloss":"错误的","context":"However, Nora understood why vulnerable residents believed the false account.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"crucial","gloss":"决定性的","context":"A sharp distinction emerged between a minor error and a crucial omission.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"permanent","gloss":"永恒的","context":"A tall photograph of a damaged tower looked genuine, and a brief caption described a permanent collapse.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tall","gloss":"高的","context":"A tall photograph of a damaged tower looked genuine, and a brief caption described a permanent collapse.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"visual","gloss":"看的","context":"The image was visual evidence of something, but it was not necessarily evidence of this particular claim.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"minor","gloss":"较小的","context":"A sharp distinction emerged between a minor error and a crucial omission.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"superior","gloss":"优良的","context":"The prime responsibility was to help people act sensibly, rather than to prove that officials were superior to anxious citizens.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"prime","gloss":"首要的","context":"The prime responsibility was to help people act sensibly, rather than to prove that officials were superior to anxious citizens.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"profound","gloss":"深刻的","context":"The change was rare enough to attract attention, yet its meaning was profound.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":{"en":"a profound change","zh":"深刻的变化"}},{"word":"radical","gloss":"根本的","context":"Contrary to popular expectations, verification did not always require radical technology.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"valid","gloss":"合理的","context":"Members compared raw reports with relevant public records and asked whether each conclusion was valid.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"genuine","gloss":"真的","context":"A tall photograph of a damaged tower looked genuine, and a brief caption described a permanent collapse.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"initial","gloss":"起初的","context":"The warning spread worldwide through similar networks, even though its initial source was obscure.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"latter","gloss":"后者","context":"Both speed and accuracy mattered, but the latter deserved careful protection during emergencies.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"supreme","gloss":"最高的","context":"Information quality was not simply a contest for the supreme voice on a screen.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"thin","gloss":"不足的","context":"Constant changes in public advice had weakened confidence, and the usual official response often seemed thin on practical detail.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"diverse","gloss":"多种多样的","context":"Reliable communication needed adequate information about specific risks, delivered in a form that diverse audiences could understand.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"soft","gloss":"温和的","context":"A soft response could preserve trust while challenging harmful advice.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"grand","gloss":"宏伟的","context":"The group rejected a grand promise that misinformation could be removed entirely.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"badly","gloss":"糟糕","context":"A weak network could transmit messages quickly but still fail badly at helping people understand them.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"A typical message in a virtual neighborhood chat group claimed that an extreme storm would destroy the city's water supply. The warning spread worldwide through similar networks, even though its initial source was obscure. A tall photograph of a damaged tower looked genuine, and a brief caption described a permanent collapse. The image was visual evidence of something, but it was not necessarily evidence of this particular claim. One resident, Nora, remained cool enough to ask where and when it had been taken. Her simple question exposed the difference between an alarming appearance and accurate information.","zh":"虚拟邻里群里的典型消息宣称极端暴风雨将摧毁城市供水。类似网络让警告传遍全球，最初来源却不明。高塔受损的照片看似真实，简短说明称其永久倒塌。图像证明了某事发生，却未必支持这条特定说法。居民诺拉冷静追问拍摄时间地点，揭示惊人外表与准确信息之间的差别。"},{"en":"A convenient search revealed that the tower stood in a remote country. The local water system was stable, and the city had issued an excellent explanation of its emergency preparations. However, Nora understood why vulnerable residents believed the false account. Constant changes in public advice had weakened confidence, and the usual official response often seemed thin on practical detail. A mere correction would not address this problem. Reliable communication needed adequate information about specific risks, delivered in a form that diverse audiences could understand. The prime responsibility was to help people act sensibly, rather than to prove that officials were superior to anxious citizens.","zh":"便捷搜索显示塔在遥远国家。本市供水稳定，市政府也发布了出色的应急准备说明。但诺拉理解脆弱居民为何相信假消息：公共建议不断变化削弱信心，惯常官方回应往往实际细节不足。仅纠错不够，需要充分说明具体风险，并让不同受众看懂。首要责任是帮人理智行动，而非证明官员优于焦虑市民。"},{"en":"Nora invited a volunteer group to prepare a flexible guide for checking urgent claims. Members compared raw reports with relevant public records and asked whether each conclusion was valid. A sharp distinction emerged between a minor error and a crucial omission. A picture could be authentic while its suggested meaning was the opposite of the truth. Contrary to popular expectations, verification did not always require radical technology. Often it involved checking dates, contacting a named organization, or noticing an odd geographical detail. These small steps provided a solid basis for judgment without asking ordinary people to become professional investigators.","zh":"诺拉组织志愿者编写灵活的紧急消息核查指南。他们对照原始报道与相关记录，检验结论是否合理，清楚区分小错误与关键遗漏。照片可能真实，暗示的意义却与真相相反。与流行期待不同，核查不一定需要激进技术，通常只需查日期、联系相关组织或发现古怪地理细节。这些小步骤给判断可靠基础，不必让普通人成为专业调查者。"},{"en":"The guide also warned against treating every mistaken sender as evil. A soft response could preserve trust while challenging harmful advice. Nora thought it vital to avoid humiliating people, because embarrassed users might retreat into private groups where corrections never arrived. An empty statement that a claim was wrong was less useful than an explanation of why. Both speed and accuracy mattered, but the latter deserved careful protection during emergencies. The group rejected a grand promise that misinformation could be removed entirely. Some confusion was inevitable, although its consequences could be reduced through patient, consistent public communication.","zh":"指南也提醒别把每个误发者视为邪恶。温和回应能在纠正有害建议时维护信任。诺拉认为避免羞辱很重要，否则用户可能退入永远接收不到纠正的私群。空泛地说错误不如解释原因。速度与准确都重要，紧急时期后者尤其需要保护。小组不作彻底消除错误信息的宏大承诺，某些混乱不可避免，但耐心持续沟通可以减轻后果。"},{"en":"Months later, the neighborhood faced another weather warning. This time residents checked several sources before forwarding it, and practical preparations began without widespread panic. The change was rare enough to attract attention, yet its meaning was profound. Information quality was not simply a contest for the supreme voice on a screen. It depended on habits of inquiry and on relationships strong enough to tolerate correction. A weak network could transmit messages quickly but still fail badly at helping people understand them. The most useful protection was a community that could remain curious while taking genuine danger seriously.","zh":"几个月后又有天气警报，这次居民转发前核对多个来源，并无大规模恐慌地做好准备。变化虽少见，意义却深刻。信息质量不是争夺屏幕上最高权威，而依赖探究习惯与能容纳纠正的关系。薄弱网络即使传信快，也可能严重不能帮助理解。最有用的保护，是保持好奇且认真对待真实危险的社区。"}],"previous":61,"next":63});
